# Auto-config registration. BigQueryFinOpsSink gained a no-arg constructor in
# sprint-23 (Story 1.2) so worker-side ServiceLoader reconstruction can rebuild
# it; before that this line was registered but unconstructable, so FinOpsSink
# was unreachable through auto-config and cost recording silently fell back to
# the no-op. Same convention as BigQueryWarehouse and
# BigQueryJobControlRepository: project/region from GCP_PROJECT/GCP_LOCATION,
# gated on CULVERT_CLOUD (BigQueryDefaults).
#
# Cost table: FINOPS_DATASET (REQUIRED - no default, see
# BigQueryDefaults.finOpsDataset()) and FINOPS_TABLE (defaults to
# BigQueryFinOpsSink.DEFAULT_TABLE, "cost_metrics"). With FINOPS_DATASET unset
# the constructor throws, which since Story 1.1 is recorded as a named
# DiscoveryFailure with an actionable message rather than swallowed - other
# providers are unaffected.
#
# The (client, projectId, dataset, table) constructor is used driver-side.
com.enrichmeai.culvert.gcp.bigquery.BigQueryFinOpsSink
